{
  "_comment": [
    "Every concrete case the Codex reviews of capture: sanitized described (rounds 1-8) and commit 7458959, one row each.",
    "tests/test_regressions.py generates the regression matrix from these rows: each row in both layers (jq and Python, which",
    "must agree), and each row of a tool route also through the real hook of every adapter (claude, codex, cursor, pi) and",
    "then the sender's own pass over what the hook wrote. A rule table that regresses fails here, whichever table it is.",
    "Columns:",
    "  id       r<round>.<finding>-<name>; source: where the case comes from",
    "  route    how the input reaches the layers:",
    "             output      tool output text (command x)",
    "             structured  tool output as a JSON value",
    "             command     the tool input's command; the tool output is <<opaque>> unless output is given",
    "             input       the tool input as a JSON value (file_path, a Codex patch as input, ...)",
    "             transcript  a model event's tool call arguments, as transcript enrichment writes them (no hook sees it)",
    "             label       extra event fields (agent_name)",
    "  expect   unchanged   byte for byte, no record, not sensitive",
    "           redacted    every generated secret gone (and every absent string), the event neither sensitive nor dropped",
    "           blanked     sensitive: the text is gone, every generated secret with it (rule: the rule that blanked it)",
    "           error       the rules failed (an invalid user regex): the text is dropped, every generated secret with it",
    "           leaks       the row's limit lets a generated secret through: at least one is still there, the event neither",
    "                       sensitive nor dropped (an explicit known limit, not a defect)",
    "  limit    the id of a known limit (limits below, each described in README.md, Known limits) the row's expect follows",
    "  env, cfg, output, keep (strings that must stay), absent (literal secrets that must go), numbers (members made numbers),",
    "  layers (the input serialized into a member of each name in turn: JSON nested in a string), encode (the text",
    "  JSON-encoded n more times), wrap (the text put into wrap at {}).",
    "  strings_only: only string values are checked for leaks (a number equal to an env value stays a number: round 3, finding 8).",
    "  layers_only: a reason the row runs in the layers only, not through the adapters' hooks.",
    "Fake secrets are placeholders, generated at run time: <<name>> or <<name:n>> (its first n characters). Names: opaque (mixed",
    "case and digits), opaque2, alpha (letters only), phrase (four words), pin (4 digits), digits8, openai, anthropic, github,",
    "github2, long (302 characters), huge (20000). <<filler:n>> is n characters of benign text."
  ],
